column3:
`atualizar_media_de_publico(league)` (cdecl, game.cpp, unnamed in the map): updates the clubs' average attendance at the end of each league season. Called by the seasons loop (0x5d5ae0, at 0x5d5cfb: push league; call; add esp, 4), at the end of the season of each league of the nation (the top one and those below, through `lower_division_id()`). 
 The club's average attendance (`attendance()`, Attendance) moves with the season result, between the minimum (`min_attendance()`) and the record (`max_attendance()`). The weight `f` comes from the competition's nation (the first dword of `competition::NATION` of `competition()`): 0.1 in [`KEY_NATION_WALES`], [`KEY_NATION_REPUBLIC_OF_IRELAND`], [`KEY_NATION_NORTHERN_IRELAND`], [`KEY_NATION_AUSTRALIA`]; 0.25 in [`KEY_NATION_DENMARK`], [`KEY_NATION_FINLAND`], [`KEY_NATION_NORWAY`], [`KEY_NATION_SWEDEN`], [`KEY_NATION_UNITED_STATES`]; 0.5 in [`KEY_NATION_SCOTLAND`]; 1 in the others. `r` = the competition's reputation (`competition::REPUTATION` of the record, word; `league_comp_reputation`). The final table comes from the statistics (Comp_Stats::get_sorted_team_table `exe::comp_stats_get_sorted_team_table`, thiscall(`comp_stats()`, 1, &n, 1000), ret 0xc: 0x76-byte records, +0 the club id, `final_position()` the club's final position of the previous season (the expectation), `current_position()` the position now (the final one, at the season's end), +5 the home games [inference], +6 the summed attendance [inference]). 
 For each club (the branches in the original's order, with the same calls to virtuals `league_vtable::HAS_AUTOMATIC_PROMOTION` "has promotion" and `league_vtable::HAS_RELEGATION` "has relegation"; d = `final_position()` − `current_position()` + 1, word): 
 - champion without promotion: + (r + max(d, 0)) × 200 × f (stadium owner, `own_stadium()`) or × 100 × f; 
 - 2nd (or position 0) without promotion: + (r + max(d, 0)) × 125 × f or × 65 × f; 
 - promoted (position ≤ `promoted_count()`): by the league above ([`G_COMP_OBJECT_TABLE`][`upper_division_id()`]; without it, nothing): v = the club's `reputation()` (word) × max(r above − r, 1) × f × 0.1, at least 100; + v + draw(v) (owner) or + v; and the floor by the reputation of the league above (`raise_attendance_floor`); 
 - promotion play-off (`promotion_playoff_count()` ≠ 0 and position ≤ `promotion_playoff_count()`): with d − 1 > 0: + draw(r(d − 1) × 75 × f) + r(d − 1) × 75 × f (owner) or + draw(r(d − 1) × 25 × f) + r(d − 1) × 10 × f; otherwise + draw(r × 50 × f or r × 25 × f); with home games, the mix with the real attendance: (summed attendance / games + 4 × average) × f × 0.2; 
 - relegated (position > `club_count()` − `relegated_count()`): by the league below (without it, nothing): v = `reputation()` × min(r below − r, −1) × f × 0.2, at most −100 (with no relegation in the league below, `league::LOWER_DIVISION_ID` = −1: v = 2v − 250 − draw(750)); + v + draw(v); and the ceiling (`cap_attendance`) of 2000 (r below ≤ 7) or 3000 times r below, × f; 
 - the others: + draw(r × d × 5 × f), × 10 for the owner with d > 0 or with `reputation()` above 500 × r; the mix with the real attendance (without the weight f); the floor by reputation; and the ceiling of 2000 r (r ≤ 7), 3000 r (r ≤ 12) or 5000 r. 
 At the end of each: at least 500, and within [`min_attendance()`, `max_attendance()`]. The table is freed (free `exe::crt_free`).
